-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Into the Eagle's Nest
  Publisher   Pandora, 1987
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Into the Eagle's Nest (1987)(Pandora)(128K)[a][a].z80
  MD5         0566e3b37d49c6fa6f62e81eb883ad0c

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

  Memory      Any Next: a 1MB Next has the memory for the game. Enhanced needs
              a 1MB Next, and is not offered on a smaller one.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  The game's play area has no colour clash, so none is removed: the default
  keeps the original look. The patch adds the menu, its cheats and the Next
  start-up. Game logic is unchanged. Enhanced colours, an option on the menu,
  are below.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    The set's own colours: brown brick walls, grey and green
              soldiers, the player in green, red and tan fittings, the panel
              in blue, gold and the night sky with the castle. Menus black
              with yellow text. Nothing repainted. Source: Enhanced colours:
              Ynicky (Spec256).

  Pace        original

  Changes     1.0: the original game on the Next, start-up only, with the
              loading screen from the (128K) tape; Enhanced colours from the
              Spec256 set, off by default: tiles and text on Layer 2, moved by
              its hardware offsets, the panel as sprites; three cheats from
              the archive, tested

  Note        Keys: on the menu 1 to 4 pick controls (2 Kempston is set), 6
              sound, 7 messages, 8 level, any other key plays, then pick a
              start level with the joystick and fire. Default: the original
              game, picture and pace; whole 8x8 tiles, so no colour clash and
              none claimed fixed. Enhanced, off by default: the Spec256 set's
              colours as they are. Fits a 1MB Next. Known issues: Enhanced
              pace in JNext -2.78% to +0.04% over whole runs, slowest
              20-update stretch +0.38%; busy rooms lag less than the original;
              scrolling by rows slightly faster. The set's menus have no blue
              paper and no highlight bar, as the set has it; the WELCOME
              screen's thin box is missing. Missing: the archive's No death by
              TNT (not tested in play) and Infinite lives (no effect, the game
              has no lives); natural play to the end; hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite ammo
   2  Infinite keys
   3  No injury

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

