-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      Run by script through the real loader on a NextZXOS 26.11 card
              copy, default, Enhanced and cheats; 1.0 not yet played by the
              owner; published at his request

  Replay      Default: no hooks, every snapshot bank byte for byte in the
              .nex, unchanged from the earlier review. Enhanced: 6 scripted
              recordings, 39171 frames, 629351 hooks run original and build
              from one state each: every register including R, all 48K RAM bar
              the site bytes and the dead stack, the clock, the MMU, the
              game's ports in order: IDENTICAL; 492921 tiles, 3614 characters,
              78285 digits, 52 redraws and 576 columns against the set;
              3757248 cells against the ULA at each update's end; 12 broken
              builds caught; 640 ABI cases; the start-up exact with and
              without NEXLOAD

  Emulator    JNext 1.1.104 headless: through the real .NEXCLASH loader on a
              private NextZXOS 26.11 card copy, default, Enhanced and cheats,
              output byte for byte as nxc.py makes it, reaching play;
              15-minute soak against the original; flicker check

  Coverage    Scripted input, no human play: menus, level select, seven floors
              (some by test pokes), scrolling in all four directions, deaths
              and restarts; not natural completion

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
